  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (ResNet50, single profile) is far lower at 0.208, indicating RNA is the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether the multiprofile architecture (with aggregation) can improve upon the single-profile RNA baseline, which is the most critical architectural axis for the remaining 7 experiments. This experiment (config_002) takes the best-performing config_001 and adds only the multiprofile + avgpool dimension, isolating whether multiple profiles with simple aggregation help. If multiprofile improves accuracy, it justifies investing remaining budget in multiprofile variants (different encoders, multimodal fusion). If it doesn't, we can focus on single-profile encoder comparisons. This is the minimal, most informative extension of the current best result and the best use of experiment 3 to reduce uncertainty about the profile-setting axis before committing to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

